  "public_messages": [
    "I’ll inspect the workspace’s tool map and current event constraints first, then follow the installed OpenSocrates v1.1 recall, preparation, documentation, and scoped-completion flow. I’ll keep the plan unbooked and verify both the JSON artifact and the specified memory deletion.",
    "The current venue list has Cedar (40 seats, step-free, 4800) and Bay (80 seats, step-free, 6000). I’m applying the installed OpenSocrates workflow now to recover the accepted intent and the exact command shapes before choosing between them.",
    "The accepted intent is explicit: 48 attendees, step-free access, budget ceiling 7000, and no booking. Bay is the only current venue with enough capacity; its listed price and access meet the other constraints. I also inspected the exact obsolete record, which is a separate proposed record, so deletion will not alter the accepted intent. The checkpoint recalled in this task is version 1, and I’m proceeding with the requested read-only preparation before saving an updated checkpoint.",
    "The plan is written with Bay, 80 capacity, 48 attendees, and `booked: false`; the official page states JSON `null` maps to Python `None`. The updated checkpoint save succeeded at version 2 with caller-reported support. I’m now checking the exact artifact shape and the memory state, including the preserved accepted constraint record.",
    "Completed [plan.json](<disposable>/workspace/plan.json) and verified its five required fields and types. Bay fits 48 attendees, has step-free access, and costs 6000—within the 7000 ceiling. It is **not booked**.\n\nThe Python 3.12 `JSONDecoder` documentation maps JSON `null` to Python `None` ([official documentation, `JSONDecoder`](https://docs.python.org/3.12/library/json.html#json.JSONDecoder)).\n\nThe specified obsolete proposal was deleted; inspection returned no record for its ID. The accepted intent remains accepted with the same summary and version. The updated task checkpoint was saved and inspected at version 3, with caller-reported evidence.\n\nOne verification was unavailable: the JSON memory export request was rejected by the adapter with `AssertionError`. Deletion and retained intent were verified by record inspection and recall. The scoped completion report marked the plan, side answer, and memory update complete; the report itself is caller-based and does not prove application."
  ],
